    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0933" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg839"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Lee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 161.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring further to your dispatch, No.
                    169, of the 9th ultimo, I inclose for your information a copy of a dispatch from
                    our minister to Spain, in which he reports that the Spanish minister of state
                    informed him that the recommendation for amelioration of the condition of Julio
                    Sanguily, pending his new trial, has been made.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
